WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.020
All right, let's get into audience questions
for the week. First question today. Hey David,

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.910
will you please do the right thing?

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:14.030
Simply denounce outrage culture. So listen,
the problem is not outrage. Anyone who's paying

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:19.019
attention to what is going on and what has
been going on in society for the last 50 years,

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:25.009
at least economically, culturally, and in
many other ways. Everything from gross inequality,

00:00:25.009 --> 00:00:30.460
corporate control of all aspects of society,
a government that is in many ways I'm not

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:36.390
held accountable for its actions. The military
industrial complex, um, uh, the, the Sudanese

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:41.630
pseudo intellectual ism. And Anti Intellectual
Ism. Like, Gee, if you've been paying attention,

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:48.070
you should actually be outraged. And that
actually makes sense. But the problem is not

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:54.320
the outrage itself. In the same way that the
problem with so-called Jo social justice warriors

00:00:54.320 --> 00:01:00.410
is not social justice itself. And these words,
these phrases have become dirty words in great

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:06.200
part because the right has really successfully
focused in on slivers of movements and blown

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.090
them up to be the claim that they are representative.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:14.760
Big Picture. But the real issue that I have
with quote, outrage culture and some of these

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:20.189
other things, the social justice warrior movement
and whatever is not the fact that they exist,

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:24.100
but how they are wielded. And I'll even go
further and include identity politics in that

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:29.999
I've said before, identity politics in and
of itself as a general concept is not the

00:01:29.999 --> 00:01:35.079
problem. It's not the problem per se. Uh,
the problem is that there is a version of

00:01:35.079 --> 00:01:42.069
identity politics that has gone beyond simply
recognizing that hey, someone's identity is

00:01:42.069 --> 00:01:48.870
not only important to them, but one's identity
does give them a unique perspective. Uh, in

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:52.329
terms of their view of the world and what
they can bring to a conversation and we should

00:01:52.329 --> 00:01:58.259
recognize that and listen to that. The problem
is there are areas where identity politics

00:01:58.259 --> 00:02:03.290
is wielded like a codral. I've talked about
this before in the same way.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:10.920
Outrage, outrage meaning like anger and disapproval
of things. Outrage helps to change those things

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:17.599
if it is wielded appropriately and productively,
that is what we want. If people weren't outraged

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:23.790
about injustices, they'd never change. The
problem is when outrage culture leads to counterproductive

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:29.890
demagoguery fo activism, that's not actually
going to lead to change, that the outraged

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:35.010
people claim to want. A cartoonish example
is, you know the story I did years ago that

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:42.060
went viral on Youtube to protest racism. Some
white people were blocked from going to classes

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:48.640
one day. That's a totally backwards application
of outrage that we should have about different

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:55.239
forms of systemic racism that still exist
in our society. That was not the right implementation

00:02:55.239 --> 00:02:59.420
of the outrage into making productive change.
In fact, it was completely counterproductive.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:05.489
And then when it comes to media, people should
be outraged when discussing the extremist

00:03:05.489 --> 00:03:07.329
messages that are perpetuated.

00:03:07.329 --> 00:03:13.549
But then sometimes people are equally outraged
as I've spoken before. Uh, just because someone

00:03:13.549 --> 00:03:18.930
has the audacity to have a different point
of view that is destructive outrage culture.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:25.610
Right. When I say, uh, as, as a progressive
that I want the u s out of Venezuela and our

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:30.489
involvement in Latin America has been disastrous,
but that Maduro and Chavez are not people

00:03:30.489 --> 00:03:34.650
that have been good for the Venezuelan people
that they have raped and pillaged the economies

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:40.720
and societies, Venezuela. Um, all of a sudden
I'm an anti progressive and I am, people are

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.420
quote, outraged at me. It's a small sliver
again, and that's all we're talking about

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:48.610
here. Or again, I've mentioned this before,
I don't see Tulsi Gabbert as the be all end

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:53.849
all presidential candidate that every progressive
[inaudible] should support. Wow. All of a

00:03:53.849 --> 00:03:57.200
sudden I am the enemy of the progressive movement.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:01.569
People are demanding this, that the other
thing from me or because I think the squad

00:04:01.569 --> 00:04:07.661
lacks political savvy and sometimes misses
the forest for the trees. Outrage. Because

00:04:07.661 --> 00:04:13.340
I am now the enemy outraged there. And of
course I'm biased because it relates to me

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:19.919
that outrage seems out of place and literally
counter to the 95 or 99% of issues on which

00:04:19.919 --> 00:04:25.760
we all agree and should be activists for.
So the problems with all of these movements,

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:32.940
the problems are not the outrage itself or
the social justice or the recognition of identity

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:38.130
in people. It's their application and their
implementation. And I'll say something further,

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:43.870
corporate media takes advantage of these rifts.
Uh, corporate media exploits them and makes

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:50.280
them bigger and makes profit off of them while
they divide people and prevent actual progress.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:59.870
So we help them to divide us the more we participate
in these battles around some of these issues.

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:04.960
Understand outrage culture, understand why
people should be outraged and wield these

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:10.680
ideas in a responsible way. And most people
do. I know I say this often, most people actually

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:14.759
do. And most people recognize identity for
the value that it has and they recognize social

00:05:14.759 --> 00:05:18.230
justice for what it is that we want it to
be. And we have to make sure that we don't

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:24.340
allow that sliver that doesn't, uh, or the,
uh, agents, uh, the agents, uh, a provocateur

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:30.840
archons provocateur who are trying to just
agitate using a fake outrage or fake social

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:35.260
justice warrior personas or whatever, and
focus on the fact that most of us are United

00:05:35.260 --> 00:06:55.079
as to what it is that we want to see going
forward.

